WEBVTT

00:00:03.910 --> 00:00:06.330
The AV-98,
aka the Ingram patrol labor.

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:09.450
6.02 tons.
8.02 meters high.

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:13.630
SCB powered.
SCLM drive system.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.920
Armed and ready for combat with a
37 millimeter revolver and stun baton.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:20.470
Designed specifically
for police use...

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.130
to make a psychological impact
on the community...

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:26.470
to deter criminals
while making the public feel safe.

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:52.210
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:55.000
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.010
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:04.380
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:07.220
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:12.230
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:19.440
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:26.200
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:32.370
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:38.210
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:44.720
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:50.390
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:01.570
A Voice in the Darkness

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:40.560
Oh, not another one.

00:02:53.410 --> 00:02:54.740
Incredible.

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:58.080
It looks like it's about to collapse.

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:00.790
Part of it already has.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:11.590
This doesn't look very good for
the training... it's too run-down.

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:14.470
It may be old, but it should do fine...

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:16.520
as long as the building can handle it.

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:19.350
The support structures are reinforced.

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:22.770
It should hold together pretty well.

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:27.360
Shinshi, give me a hand!

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:32.740
The question is how well the Labors
will function inside the building.

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:34.700
We're bringing them inside?

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:38.710
Yes. Fortunately, we only
need rough data,

00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:43.380
so we can help with demolition
while we're training.

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:47.550
Captain, this really isn't
a job for the police.

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:51.680
That's why you don't have to
worry about making mistakes.

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:55.680
We have several training goals here:
Urban combat,

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:59.310
disaster relief, and general
experience with condemned buildings.

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:02.650
Those sound like worthwhile goals to me.

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:05.150
So we might as well enjoy ourselves.

00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:09.030
First, we'll remove anything of value.

00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:14.990
Work on dexterity with
your Labors whenever you can.

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:17.700
Move out.

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:22.120
Okay, let's get to work.

00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:29.340
Is it high enough?

00:04:30.130 --> 00:04:33.800
Asuma, do we have room to stand up?

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:38.260
The ceiling in this hall is
incredibly high. You'll be fine.

00:04:39.430 --> 00:04:40.770
We're going in.

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:51.490
Start by taking down this painting.

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:57.580
I don't know very much about art.

00:04:57.580 --> 00:05:00.620
Should I be really careful,
or is it okay to be rough?

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:04.080
Captain, do you know?

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:06.000
Don't ask me.

00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:10.210
I'm sure the valuable paintings
were removed long ago.

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:13.550
Sounds good to me!
Let's trash the place!

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:30.190
Ota, wait!

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:31.780
What?

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:34.240
What's wrong, Izumi?

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:37.950
I like that painting.

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:49.540
What a gloomy dump.

00:05:57.720 --> 00:06:00.680
Looks fine here.
Let's check the second floor.

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:03.930
Hurry up, it's almost dark.

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:06.640
Well, so long Ota.

00:06:07.230 --> 00:06:09.020
You're leaving now?

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:09.940
Yeah.

00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:12.360
Have fun on the night shift.

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:13.480
Sorry.

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:20.490
What are you doing
on the next day off?

00:06:20.910 --> 00:06:22.240
Why?

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:25.160
Oh, I don't know.
You want to go see a movie?

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:28.790
That's before payday. Your treat?

00:06:29.290 --> 00:06:31.630
Before payday?
You're right, I forgot about that.

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:34.130
It's okay... we'll go Dutch.

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:36.630
It must be nice to be young.

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:49.600
Yes?

00:07:21.090 --> 00:07:23.180
Well, that's it for us.

00:07:23.180 --> 00:07:24.430
Thank you for your help.

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:30.980
I don't mean to pry, but are
you really staying here tonight?

00:07:30.980 --> 00:07:32.980
Yes, we're working through the night.

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:36.480
I see. Well... be careful.

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:40.450
Man, cops sure are brave!

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:42.490
They're a rare breed.

00:07:42.490 --> 00:07:44.330
What courage!

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:45.280
What was that about?

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:46.450
No idea.

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:22.410
...moreover, its merits
as a multi-use machine...

00:08:28.660 --> 00:08:29.450
Huh?

00:08:45.970 --> 00:08:47.970
HELP   HELP   HELP

00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:47.970
Help?

00:08:58.940 --> 00:09:00.990
What's going on?

00:09:41.730 --> 00:09:43.110
And who are you?

00:10:16.270 --> 00:10:17.730
Who's there?

00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:18.770
What's wrong?

00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:21.820
It felt like someone
was tugging on me.

00:10:22.190 --> 00:10:23.030
It's your imagination.

00:10:23.030 --> 00:10:24.320
But...

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:27.070
Who can move an Ingram?

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:28.320
That's true...

00:10:36.580 --> 00:10:38.210
But I was so sure...

00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:43.170
I'm back.

00:10:47.550 --> 00:10:52.890
Ota, they only had one hirekatsu left,
so the other is deep-fried.

00:10:53.220 --> 00:10:54.720
Which do you want?

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:55.810
HIREKATSU!

00:10:55.810 --> 00:10:59.400
Don't snap at me.
I won't take it from you.

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:00.480
Shut up!

00:11:01.440 --> 00:11:03.190
What's with him?

00:11:03.520 --> 00:11:07.900
Beats me. Let's go upstairs.
The Captain's waiting for dinner.

00:11:37.850 --> 00:11:38.890
Captain!

00:11:40.390 --> 00:11:42.020
Dinner's here!

00:11:45.980 --> 00:11:48.780
Captain, what are you doing?

00:11:48.780 --> 00:11:50.200
Can't you see?

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:51.570
No...

00:11:54.280 --> 00:11:55.740
Oh, I see.

00:11:56.870 --> 00:11:58.660
I guess you can't.

00:11:59.250 --> 00:12:05.250
I just thought... that I needed some
exercise before dinner.

00:12:08.380 --> 00:12:10.260
Well, dinner's here.

00:12:11.090 --> 00:12:11.970
Oh?

00:12:15.470 --> 00:12:21.100
So while you're napping,
Captain, what should I do?

00:12:21.520 --> 00:12:24.230
Stay right here.
I'll be awake in a couple of hours.

00:12:55.180 --> 00:12:57.760
There's something strange
about this place.

00:12:58.060 --> 00:12:59.720
Yeah... what?

00:12:59.720 --> 00:13:01.390
It feels like someone's living here.

00:13:02.140 --> 00:13:05.480
No way! It's been abandoned for years.

00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:08.070
Maybe there's a stray cat around,
or some transient.

00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:14.700
No, it's more than that.
It just feels like someone lives here.

00:13:14.700 --> 00:13:15.700
What are you talking about?

00:13:18.030 --> 00:13:19.540
I'm not sure myself.

00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:28.840
You know, I've been getting strange
feelings around here. It comes and goes.

00:13:28.840 --> 00:13:30.460
So you agree, Ota?

00:13:31.090 --> 00:13:38.720
It makes sense. A lot of people
died here, in the last quake.

00:13:38.720 --> 00:13:42.560
You mean the Tokyo Bay quake?

00:13:42.560 --> 00:13:48.860
Yeah, about four years back.
The ground turned to quicksand.

00:13:48.860 --> 00:13:51.030
It got pretty gruesome.

00:13:51.530 --> 00:13:53.240
Was it that bad?

00:13:53.740 --> 00:13:55.200
Didn't you hear about it?

00:13:56.950 --> 00:14:01.290
If any place deserves to be haunted,
it's this old mansion.

00:14:02.660 --> 00:14:04.040
By the way, Izumi...

00:14:04.040 --> 00:14:07.250
Does your Ingram seem kind of sluggish?

00:14:07.250 --> 00:14:09.630
You're having trouble with yours too?

00:14:10.670 --> 00:14:15.970
Ever since we got here.
And the Captain's acting weird too.

00:14:16.260 --> 00:14:17.720
I don't like it.

00:14:59.430 --> 00:15:07.310
I talked to the local residents...
they say this place is haunted.

00:15:08.850 --> 00:15:13.860
They all told the same story,
about a night watchman,

00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:17.650
who was walking by before the
fence was put up for demolition work.

00:15:19.150 --> 00:15:24.870
He saw lots of people in traditional clothing,
and thought they were filming a historical drama.

00:15:29.790 --> 00:15:32.040
But when he looked closer...

00:15:36.210 --> 00:15:37.130
They had no legs.

00:15:44.850 --> 00:15:46.220
Typical for ghosts!

00:15:46.220 --> 00:15:48.430
The one I saw wasn't like that.

00:15:48.430 --> 00:15:50.390
What?!!!

00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:53.060
Oh, never mind!

00:15:53.610 --> 00:15:54.400
You saw one?

00:15:54.690 --> 00:15:55.980
You DID see something!

00:15:55.980 --> 00:15:58.990
It's nothing! Don't worry about it.

00:15:58.990 --> 00:16:00.650
Tell us!

00:16:00.650 --> 00:16:02.030
Spill the beans!

00:16:02.030 --> 00:16:03.820
I told you... it's nothing.

00:16:04.490 --> 00:16:07.450
Why are you even discussing this
superstitious nonsense?

00:16:09.330 --> 00:16:13.630
He's the Captain!
He doesn't have to tell you anything!

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:15.840
No need to get angry.

00:16:15.840 --> 00:16:18.710
But this is a special case!

00:16:18.960 --> 00:16:20.170
Stop it!

00:16:20.510 --> 00:16:22.550
We might as well hear the rest.

00:16:22.550 --> 00:16:23.390
But...

00:16:23.390 --> 00:16:25.850
Oh, don't worry.
Go on, Shinshi.

00:16:26.350 --> 00:16:29.180
Well, I decided to check around.

00:16:29.180 --> 00:16:31.560
You seem to have plenty of free time.

00:16:31.560 --> 00:16:34.560
Well, I was on my way
to the grocery anyway.

00:16:34.560 --> 00:16:37.780
So that's why you
were gone so long!

00:16:40.400 --> 00:16:42.820
This last earthquake was
only the most recent incident.

00:16:43.240 --> 00:16:46.950
These buildings have
always been cursed.

00:16:46.950 --> 00:16:51.330
During the war, they took
a direct hit from a bomb.

00:16:51.330 --> 00:16:56.420
And the central building fell
in the Great Kanto Earthquake.

00:16:56.710 --> 00:17:02.050
That's where the courtyard is today,
but centuries ago...

00:17:02.420 --> 00:17:06.510
back in the Tokugawa era,
it was the Mansion of the Hiura Clan.

00:17:07.930 --> 00:17:10.680
And that's just the beginning.

00:17:10.980 --> 00:17:12.480
There's more?

00:17:12.810 --> 00:17:15.150
It was "The Age of Treasures."

00:17:15.150 --> 00:17:22.110
Miyawaki, the lord here,
went insane and slew his followers.

00:17:25.820 --> 00:17:32.410
Stop this rubbish! Ghosts and curses!
It's all just nonsense!

00:17:33.080 --> 00:17:34.250
But aren't you curious?

00:17:36.250 --> 00:17:38.840
Hey, my hometown has
a ghost story too!

00:17:38.840 --> 00:17:40.170
I'm not listening to this!

00:17:44.510 --> 00:17:46.390
She's no fun!

00:17:46.390 --> 00:17:50.600
No one likes ghost stories when
there are real ghosts around.

00:18:04.150 --> 00:18:06.780
Hit! Machine 1,
your left arm is useless.

00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:10.990
Ota's a better marksman than that.

00:18:20.540 --> 00:18:22.460
That was your last bullet, Ota!

00:18:22.460 --> 00:18:23.710
Bull's eye!

00:18:27.470 --> 00:18:30.600
Hey, what's going on?

00:18:30.600 --> 00:18:31.850
What's wrong, Noa?

00:18:31.850 --> 00:18:33.020
My monitor's out.

00:18:34.020 --> 00:18:35.640
The signal's fine here.

00:18:35.640 --> 00:18:36.730
That's odd.

00:18:39.860 --> 00:18:42.570
And I was so close!

00:18:47.450 --> 00:18:50.870
How'd you get in here?
Hey, it's dangerous down there!

00:18:51.950 --> 00:18:53.410
Hey, you!

00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:04.670
What's wrong, Noa?

00:19:04.960 --> 00:19:08.260
Asuma, can you escort
that little boy out of here?

00:19:10.010 --> 00:19:12.850
Little boy? Where?

00:19:16.390 --> 00:19:19.770
Where? Huh?

00:19:23.650 --> 00:19:26.400
Will you please stop it?

00:19:27.070 --> 00:19:30.530
How long are you going
to continue this sick joke?

00:19:30.530 --> 00:19:35.160
Well it <i>is</i> odd that both
machines are responding poorly.

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:37.830
- Shall we dig?
- What?

00:19:38.210 --> 00:19:42.420
Let's dig right where the little boy
pointed. Maybe we'll find something.

00:19:42.420 --> 00:19:46.300
Captain, don't tell me you
believe in this nonsense too!

00:19:46.300 --> 00:19:50.130
I must admit, I'm curious.
I did see something.

00:19:50.720 --> 00:19:52.180
Impossible!

00:19:53.510 --> 00:19:54.720
You look pale!

00:19:56.060 --> 00:19:57.720
Do I?

00:19:59.560 --> 00:20:01.560
Lieutenant! Behind you!

00:20:05.230 --> 00:20:07.990
Stop it! Stop! Please!

00:20:09.190 --> 00:20:12.160
Stop! Stop! Please stop it!

00:20:16.450 --> 00:20:20.790
Please stop!
I hate this kind of stuff!

00:20:22.670 --> 00:20:24.290
That was unexpected.

00:20:24.290 --> 00:20:26.130
It was too much for her.

00:20:26.130 --> 00:20:27.340
Cute.

00:20:27.340 --> 00:20:27.920
Huh?

00:20:30.340 --> 00:20:33.090
Ota, how's your Ingram handling?

00:20:33.090 --> 00:20:35.430
Seems okay. Yours?

00:20:36.220 --> 00:20:39.680
Mine's fine too.
So what happened before?

00:20:48.940 --> 00:20:49.990
Ota!

00:20:51.450 --> 00:20:53.990
- Ota!
- Are you okay, Ota?!

00:20:58.290 --> 00:20:59.790
What is this?

00:21:34.530 --> 00:21:39.990
Special Vehicles uncovers 200-year-old crime

00:21:35.160 --> 00:21:39.990
Lord Hiura killed dozens of his
retainers in an insane rage.

00:21:40.240 --> 00:21:46.330
But he told the Shogun they'd been
injured in an accident.

00:21:46.330 --> 00:21:48.920
And then he secretly disposed of the
bodies?

00:21:48.920 --> 00:21:51.760
Exactly.
He used an old forgotten tunnel.

00:21:53.220 --> 00:21:57.140
So their anger is what
triggered all the later disasters?

00:21:57.140 --> 00:22:00.930
The newspaper doesn't mention
that aspect, but it's possible.

00:22:01.680 --> 00:22:05.270
I see. So the more recent ghosts were trying
to help you find the original victims...

00:22:05.270 --> 00:22:10.730
in order to calm their
anger and suffering.

00:22:10.730 --> 00:22:13.280
Well... they could've expressed
themselves a bit better.

00:22:13.610 --> 00:22:17.320
So you did a volunteer job
for a bunch of ghosts.

00:22:18.450 --> 00:22:20.330
That's quite a community service.

00:22:20.910 --> 00:22:22.620
Yeah, I guess so.

00:22:22.620 --> 00:22:29.840
No trespassing
No dumping garbage

00:22:43.020 --> 00:22:46.230
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:22:46.350 --> 00:22:49.940
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:22:52.270 --> 00:22:56.190
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:03.620 --> 00:23:05.700
yume ni hikizurare
Pulled into my dream I find that I wake up

00:23:05.830 --> 00:23:08.620
ore wa ase mamire no Lonely
Drenched in sweat and feeling lonely

00:23:08.710 --> 00:23:13.210
hanashi-aite no TV suitchi hipparu
I turn off the TV I've been listening to

00:23:15.880 --> 00:23:17.880
ashita ichinichi wa
Tomorrow I will spend the whole day

00:23:17.970 --> 00:23:20.720
akogareta machi no gomi no naka
In the city of my dreams, amidst the old dust

00:23:20.970 --> 00:23:24.890
hayaku mein sutoriito ni sawaritai no sa
I want to feel the main street beneath my feet soon

00:23:28.060 --> 00:23:31.400
manazashi dake wa itsu demo
I plan to always look on the brighter side

00:23:34.020 --> 00:23:36.650
ue wo muite 'ru tsumori
Keep my chin up, look to the future

00:23:36.610 --> 00:23:39.200
tatta hitotsu no michi da kara
After all, there's only one path I can travel

00:23:39.200 --> 00:23:42.410
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:23:42.660 --> 00:23:46.500
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:23:48.870 --> 00:23:52.670
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:54.840 --> 00:23:58.720
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:24:01.050 --> 00:24:05.350
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:24:06.850 --> 00:24:10.020
This story is fiction...

00:24:06.850 --> 00:24:10.020
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:16.480 --> 00:24:18.490
Days off are for playing games
and watching movies.

00:24:18.490 --> 00:24:23.450
I tried playing a Patlabor video game,
but I got my butt kicked.

00:24:23.450 --> 00:24:24.280
That's so annoying!!

00:24:24.280 --> 00:24:27.120
Here comes some mysterious guy
from out of nowhere...

00:24:27.120 --> 00:24:28.950
who's an absolute master of the game.

00:24:28.950 --> 00:24:32.750
This strange old guy seems to be in
cahoots with some cute little boy.

00:24:32.750 --> 00:24:34.540
What a strange combination.

00:24:34.540 --> 00:24:38.090
Next Episode, "The Suspicious Pair"
Target, Locked On!

00:24:37.590 --> 00:24:42.590
Next episode

00:24:37.590 --> 00:24:42.590
The Suspicious Pair
